  "historical_output_text": " One pattern we commonly encounter around here are those days after warm, calm, clear days. It can feel nice on those initial calm and still warm nights - it can even seem quite nice in early-moming as you step outside to take out trash.\n\nThen you might see the wind suddenly increase, often accompanied with cloudier conditions and possibly drizzly rain too - and those days tend last only about one full calendar date - maybe one day at the maximum before they are gone - before it goes calm.\n\nWhy?\n\nWhen warm weather persists and conditions stay still - like no strong high pressures and calm low pressures around - that air tends not to hold moisture and so doesn.imgur't show the sky is cloudy - it tends to dry and warm up more - like if you left wet terry-cloth in full sunlight.\n\nAs soon the pressure or wind starts changing and",
